WEBVTT

00:01.950 --> 00:04.030
What are those marks? How horrible...

00:04.030 --> 00:05.020
How disgusting.

00:05.020 --> 00:06.300
Don't touch me...

00:08.800 --> 00:11.460
D-Don't get any closer to me.

00:11.460 --> 00:13.360
Get away from me...

00:13.360 --> 00:14.390
It's me!

00:14.390 --> 00:15.590
Futaki-san!

00:18.320 --> 00:20.390
Naoe...?

00:22.520 --> 00:23.700
Onee-chan!

00:28.870 --> 00:30.480
Why did you come here?

00:30.480 --> 00:32.530
What do you mean?

00:32.530 --> 00:35.610
Please just... leave me alone...

00:54.050 --> 00:55.320
How pathetic.

00:57.100 --> 00:58.320
I'm the worst.

00:59.870 --> 01:05.970
Our Bonds

01:16.360 --> 01:17.700
Futaki-san!

01:19.560 --> 01:21.450
Maybe she didn't hear me?

01:21.450 --> 01:22.470
Riki!

01:23.260 --> 01:25.860
Did you see Kanata-san just now?

01:25.860 --> 01:27.330
Yeah, but she just left.

01:27.840 --> 01:29.920
I see...

01:29.920 --> 01:32.450
She's been avoiding me all morning.

01:32.450 --> 01:35.590
She probably doesn't want to make anyone worry.

01:36.920 --> 01:37.880
Did you hear?

01:37.880 --> 01:39.180
The rumors about Futaki-san.

01:39.660 --> 01:41.600
You mean her burns?

01:41.600 --> 01:44.750
Apparently, those marks aren't burns.

01:44.750 --> 01:45.740
Really?

01:45.740 --> 01:48.560
Could they be from abuse?

01:50.140 --> 01:51.400
Riki...

01:52.720 --> 01:56.960
Only a few people should know about what happened yesterday.

01:57.800 --> 01:58.910
Physical abuse?

01:58.910 --> 02:00.320
From who?

02:00.320 --> 02:01.950
Well, the public morals chairman...

02:14.920 --> 02:15.890
What's this?

02:15.210 --> 02:16.640
Dorm Head's Room

02:15.230 --> 02:16.660
Dorm Head's Room

02:15.890 --> 02:17.880
You're helping me out again today?

02:18.520 --> 02:19.420
Yeah.

02:19.420 --> 02:21.620
Thank goodness, I needed a hand.

02:27.660 --> 02:29.690
Is this Futaki-san's?

02:30.500 --> 02:31.380
What happened?

02:31.380 --> 02:32.700
Did you two have a fight or something?

02:33.380 --> 02:34.640
Just kidding.

02:34.640 --> 02:36.110
She's not coming today.

02:36.680 --> 02:38.740
It must be hard for her to face anyone right now.

02:40.320 --> 02:40.360
Naoe Riki,

02:40.320 --> 02:40.360
I have ironed the shirt

02:40.320 --> 02:40.360
and....

02:45.080 --> 02:47.160
The club room has been secured.

02:47.160 --> 02:48.140
Really?

02:48.640 --> 02:50.000
Yahoo!

02:50.000 --> 02:51.690
I'm as happy as the rest of you.

02:51.690 --> 02:53.480
And it's all thanks to everyone's effort.

02:53.480 --> 02:55.710
We have to make sure to thank Futaki as well.

02:56.200 --> 02:58.920
Yeah, she gave us a huge helping hand.

02:58.920 --> 03:00.840
What? She's surprisingly a good person.

03:03.240 --> 03:04.870
Are you worried about Futaki?

03:04.870 --> 03:05.980
Yeah.

03:07.500 --> 03:09.550
The clubroom matter's done.

03:09.550 --> 03:11.900
But you should visit the dorm committee again.

03:11.900 --> 03:13.400
I'm sure the dorm head will be delighted.

03:14.120 --> 03:15.690
Yeah, probably.

03:29.240 --> 03:30.830
You know, about onee-chan...

03:30.830 --> 03:35.390
No matter how busy she is, she still does perfectly well on her schoolwork.

03:36.140 --> 03:39.500
But lately she hasn't been paying attention to the teacher at all.

03:40.180 --> 03:43.070
She always looks so out of it during class.

03:43.070 --> 03:45.340
Maybe she hasn't been sleeping?

03:45.700 --> 03:50.890
Onee-chan hasn't said anything, but I'm pretty sure she's bothered by the rumors.

03:51.700 --> 03:53.470
Let's go and talk with her.

03:53.470 --> 03:55.860
We might be able to help her somehow.

04:02.100 --> 04:04.820
The time of the meeting is unchanged, but...

04:05.420 --> 04:08.590
Your relatives were terribly angry with you.

04:10.400 --> 04:12.410
It was entirely your own fault.

04:12.410 --> 04:14.940
Messing up right before the engagement...

04:14.940 --> 04:16.090
What did you say?

04:18.220 --> 04:19.730
Haruka.

04:19.730 --> 04:21.670
What do you mean "engagement?"

04:21.670 --> 04:23.630
I didn't hear anything about that! What's the meaning of this?!

04:25.000 --> 04:26.590
It has nothing to do with you, Haruka.

04:27.430 --> 04:28.680
Onee-chan!

04:40.000 --> 04:41.180
Is my sister...

04:41.180 --> 04:42.450
getting married?

04:44.510 --> 04:46.030
Is my sister getting married?!

04:48.100 --> 04:50.100
By the end of summer,

04:50.100 --> 04:51.670
with someone from the Saigusa family.

04:51.670 --> 04:52.780
Does that mean—

04:52.780 --> 04:56.460
She will become the heiress to both the Futaki and Saigusa families.

04:56.970 --> 04:58.190
Why?

04:58.190 --> 05:00.970
If she gets married, she won't be able to leave that household!

05:00.970 --> 05:03.700
She'll be stuck there...

05:03.700 --> 05:04.920
forever.

05:06.180 --> 05:07.430
It's for your sake, you know.

05:21.920 --> 05:25.400
How does it feel to swing a shinai you don't want to wield?

05:25.680 --> 05:27.250
It doesn't concern you.

05:27.250 --> 05:28.380
Leave me alone.

05:40.960 --> 05:43.090
I'm asking you how it feels.

05:44.450 --> 05:46.300
It hurts my arm.

05:48.650 --> 05:51.300
You won't be able to defeat anything with that sword.

05:52.180 --> 05:54.460
I know that already...

05:54.460 --> 05:56.220
You don't have to tell me.

05:58.840 --> 06:00.040
Sorry for barging in.

06:13.100 --> 06:17.440
Haruka lost again. She really is hopeless.

06:18.630 --> 06:22.430
Kanata, you're the winner. Congratulations.

06:22.430 --> 06:24.460
We're done comparing.

06:24.950 --> 06:25.780
Yes, sir.

06:25.780 --> 06:29.180
I'll do my best to not disappoint you.

06:30.430 --> 06:31.970
What's going to happen to her?

06:32.820 --> 06:34.600
I'm not asking out of sympathy.

06:34.600 --> 06:36.650
I'm just curious.

06:37.580 --> 06:40.200
Will Saigusa be abandoned?

06:40.200 --> 06:43.080
No, forget I asked.

06:56.080 --> 06:56.790
Haruka?!

07:14.930 --> 07:16.150
Stop!

07:17.530 --> 07:20.930
I won't mess up the next one.

07:21.300 --> 07:22.920
I'll do my best next time...

07:22.050 --> 07:23.400
Stop it, Kanata!

07:23.400 --> 07:25.820
I promise I'll do my best...

07:24.600 --> 07:26.230
What did you do...

07:26.230 --> 07:28.510
What the hell did you do to my Haruka?!

07:28.510 --> 07:29.890
You promised me, didn't you?!

07:29.890 --> 07:33.020
That if I did my best, you would leave Haruka alone!

07:33.020 --> 07:33.950
So what the hell is this?!

07:33.950 --> 07:36.080
What is the meaning of this?!

07:37.550 --> 07:39.080
Answer me.

07:40.660 --> 07:42.520
Say something!

07:42.520 --> 07:46.250
The Saigusa family needed to be treated accordingly.

07:46.250 --> 07:48.420
For bringing misfortune into ours.

07:49.540 --> 07:51.050
This is just wrong.

07:51.050 --> 07:55.030
All of you were telling me how you wanted to stop with these weird customs.

07:56.270 --> 07:57.310
Come on.

07:57.310 --> 07:58.780
Someone else speak up.

07:59.630 --> 08:01.430
You guys agreed with me earlier, didn't you?

08:01.810 --> 08:04.950
"This is wrong, we need to change things." is what you said.

08:04.950 --> 08:06.440
Isn't that right?

08:08.610 --> 08:09.780
Why isn't anyone saying anything?!

08:09.780 --> 08:11.380
Why?!

08:11.380 --> 08:14.220
There's no need or reason to change anything.

08:14.220 --> 08:16.290
Things are fine the way they are right now.

08:16.290 --> 08:18.300
Our number one Kanata.

08:18.300 --> 08:20.730
You're not our representative.

08:21.240 --> 08:22.730
Not yet, at least.

08:23.880 --> 08:25.670
What are you trying to say?

08:27.060 --> 08:30.120
There's only one way you can save your sister.

08:30.680 --> 08:33.800
From this point on, abandon your own future.

08:34.360 --> 08:38.370
If you do that, then we'll free your sister immediately.

08:41.610 --> 08:44.010
Do you really think I'll accept those conditions?

08:44.010 --> 08:45.180
You're right.

08:45.180 --> 08:47.400
Everyone likes to think they're special.

08:47.400 --> 08:50.730
Back when I asked if you wanted to switch places with Haruka,

08:50.730 --> 08:52.650
You didn't nod, did you?

08:53.440 --> 08:54.680
That's—

08:59.350 --> 09:01.490
What is it that you want, Kanata?

09:10.960 --> 09:12.370
If I agree with your conditions...

09:13.820 --> 09:15.980
If I let go of my future...

09:17.550 --> 09:20.470
Will you really save her?

09:21.240 --> 09:22.470
Yeah.

09:24.180 --> 09:28.980
Will you swear to never harm her again?

09:29.770 --> 09:30.610
Yeah.

09:31.570 --> 09:34.360
Is it okay if she goes to school too?

09:34.630 --> 09:35.570
Yeah.

09:35.570 --> 09:36.610
Then...

09:37.900 --> 09:40.680
Would it be all right...

09:40.680 --> 09:43.700
if I held Haruka's hand–

09:43.700 --> 09:44.700
That is prohibited.

09:52.580 --> 09:54.580
But for now...

09:55.700 --> 09:57.540
I'm able to save Haruka.

10:01.830 --> 10:02.860
All right.

10:03.440 --> 10:06.820
I'll agree to your conditions.

10:10.490 --> 10:12.040
My beloved Haruka.

10:12.760 --> 10:14.260
My precious Haruka.

10:15.630 --> 10:18.410
My baby sister.

10:31.080 --> 10:31.850
Good morning!

10:31.850 --> 10:33.130
I'll change your towel for you.

10:35.760 --> 10:36.860
Are you all right?

10:36.860 --> 10:40.820
You passed out from your fever. You were probably just overworking yourself.

10:41.630 --> 10:43.050
So, what of it?

10:43.350 --> 10:47.810
Me being overworked isn't something you need to be concerned about.

10:47.810 --> 10:49.060
It has nothing to do with you.

10:49.910 --> 10:53.130
That may be so, but I'm still worried about you.

10:53.130 --> 10:54.040
Why?

10:54.040 --> 10:56.060
Because I am.

10:56.060 --> 10:57.910
You have no reason to be concerned.

10:57.910 --> 11:00.110
I don't need a reason to be worried about you.

11:02.710 --> 11:03.740
I don't care anymore.

11:04.020 --> 11:05.320
Why not?

11:05.820 --> 11:08.140
Your hand is small.

11:08.700 --> 11:10.890
So is mine, and everyone else's.

11:10.890 --> 11:13.070
Our hands are small and frail.

11:13.070 --> 11:16.460
We don't know if we'll be able to hold and protect even a single thing.

11:17.040 --> 11:21.560
What do you think will happen to those who carelessly extend their hands to help others?

11:24.140 --> 11:27.470
Let's say there are two people who are about to fall off a cliff.

11:27.470 --> 11:31.100
You see them and you want to save both of them.

11:34.880 --> 11:37.270
But if you do, you'll fall off the cliff yourself.

11:38.190 --> 11:40.380
That would be stupid, right?

11:40.380 --> 11:44.120
So, don't extend your hand to me.

11:44.120 --> 11:45.980
Don't concern yourself with me.

11:45.980 --> 11:46.660
Futaki-sa–

11:46.660 --> 11:48.530
I've always done things by myself.

11:48.530 --> 11:51.150
I didn't live up to this point being protected by you.

11:51.150 --> 11:53.170
I've never had anyone to stand by my side.

11:53.530 --> 11:56.660
I've never had anyone to come to my rescue.

11:57.240 --> 12:00.460
No one came to even hold me or comfort me.

12:02.030 --> 12:04.440
What good will it do now?

12:05.340 --> 12:07.220
Just leave me alone.

12:11.900 --> 12:13.530
"It has nothing to do with you."

12:13.530 --> 12:15.150
"Leave me alone."

12:15.150 --> 12:19.150
I think everyone wants to yell out those words at some point.

12:19.680 --> 12:24.320
But you know, after you say those things, you'll feel scared.

12:24.320 --> 12:27.210
"What will I do if I end up all alone?"

12:27.210 --> 12:29.710
"What should I do if no one comes for me?"

12:30.630 --> 12:34.170
I'm sure you'd be happier to say: "Don't leave me."

12:34.980 --> 12:37.330
I know I was happy to say that.

12:37.330 --> 12:40.500
That's why I won't leave you alone.

12:43.530 --> 12:44.680
Kanata.

12:50.240 --> 12:51.500
There, there.

12:51.500 --> 12:52.940
You did great.

12:54.550 --> 12:56.540
You don't have to get married.

12:56.540 --> 12:58.540
You don't have to take over the family.

12:58.540 --> 13:02.150
If uncle and our relatives have a problem with that, we'll just drive them away.

13:02.930 --> 13:04.800
"We"?

13:04.800 --> 13:05.610
Yeah.

13:05.610 --> 13:08.380
Onee-chan, you're no longer alone.

13:08.380 --> 13:11.820
I'm here for you, kud is, and everyone else as well.

13:13.300 --> 13:16.920
There's no point for you to be alone for my sake.

13:18.620 --> 13:20.380
There's no point at all.

13:21.640 --> 13:24.330
I don't even know what's going to happen at this point.

13:40.620 --> 13:41.520
What are you going to do now?

13:41.860 --> 13:44.520
I'll rest for a bit, then head back to the dorms.

13:47.040 --> 13:51.640
You know, on our way to school tomorrow, do you want to walk to class together in the morning?

13:51.640 --> 13:54.620
I want to make up for the lost time.

13:55.090 --> 13:59.270
Our thoughts, things I want to ask you,
things I want to tell you...

13:59.270 --> 14:01.080
There's a lot.

14:01.640 --> 14:04.130
There are lots of things I never got to tell you.

14:09.120 --> 14:10.500
Haruka...

14:10.500 --> 14:11.530
What is it?

14:13.080 --> 14:16.270
I'm glad you brought me here.

14:17.780 --> 14:20.260
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

14:29.740 --> 14:31.260
See you tomorrow...

14:35.620 --> 14:36.840
Haruka?

14:43.760 --> 14:46.050
Thanks for helping out Onee-chan.

14:46.050 --> 14:47.620
D-Don't mention it...

14:47.620 --> 14:49.250
I didn't really do anything.

14:49.760 --> 14:52.010
Riki-kun, you really are nice.

14:52.340 --> 14:55.010
As I thought, you really are a nice person.

14:57.760 --> 14:59.190
Let's go, Riki-kun.

14:59.190 --> 15:00.310
Sure.

15:07.640 --> 15:08.570
Onee-chan!

15:10.900 --> 15:12.330
Futaki-san!

15:15.950 --> 15:18.040
Where are they taking Onee-chan?

15:19.100 --> 15:20.930
The Futaki household.

15:20.930 --> 15:22.880
She won't be coming back here.

15:22.880 --> 15:23.830
No way!

15:23.830 --> 15:26.260
If we don't hurry up and rescue her, Onee-chan will...

15:26.260 --> 15:29.130
Do you intend to defy the Futaki Household?

15:30.240 --> 15:34.020
Yeah, you can report to them if you want.

15:34.020 --> 15:38.310
Even if I have to destroy you guys, I'll rescue Onee-chan for sure.

15:41.170 --> 15:45.220
The meeting will be held tomorrow afternoon, at the hotel in the shopping district.

15:45.220 --> 15:46.190
Why are you telling me?

15:46.680 --> 15:51.010
My job was to bring Kanata-san out.

15:51.010 --> 15:53.690
I have nothing to do with this anymore.

15:56.840 --> 15:57.990
This will be difficult.

15:57.990 --> 16:00.450
I know that, but I still want to save her!

16:00.450 --> 16:02.620
I'd like to ask for everyone's help.

16:04.820 --> 16:05.750
There you have it.

16:09.320 --> 16:10.420
Everyone!

16:10.750 --> 16:13.590
Now let's go crash that party!

16:13.590 --> 16:14.370
Yeah!

16:23.530 --> 16:26.770
Take off that hair ornament already.

16:26.770 --> 16:28.720
It doesn't fit well with the dress.

16:33.320 --> 16:34.450
Let's review the plan.

16:34.990 --> 16:36.810
Here are the emergency stairs.

16:36.810 --> 16:40.210
Once the fire alarm rings, the shutters will close.

16:40.210 --> 16:41.910
The stairs are located here and here.

16:41.910 --> 16:44.710
Once the fire alarm goes off, the elevator will shut down.

16:44.710 --> 16:47.020
Which means our routes are limited.

16:47.020 --> 16:47.780
Yeah.

16:47.780 --> 16:50.670
Nishizono-san, where's that thing you asked for from the Science Club President?

16:50.670 --> 16:52.740
It is right here.

16:52.740 --> 16:56.220
All I have to do is install it on the circuit in the mechanical room, right?

16:56.220 --> 17:02.680
Yeah. First up, Nishizono-san will install the device that will allow the elevators to run.

17:03.320 --> 17:05.740
Next, the decoys will wait at the emergency staircase.

17:05.740 --> 17:07.940
You two will secure their escape route.

17:08.290 --> 17:12.150
Kuu-chan and I have to wait with the taxi, right?

17:12.440 --> 17:17.640
Then Kengo, Masato, and my job is to cause a commotion.

17:17.640 --> 17:21.540
Meanwhile, you and Haruka-kun will grab Futaki and run.

17:21.540 --> 17:22.370
Yep.

17:22.370 --> 17:24.560
My heart is beating so fast!

17:24.560 --> 17:27.170
Yeah, this is a pretty solid plan.

17:27.170 --> 17:32.130
Even so, boy, you seem like you're having a lot of fun devising this plan.

17:32.130 --> 17:33.170
Is that so?

17:33.610 --> 17:35.390
I guess so.

17:35.390 --> 17:38.290
I wonder if Kyousuke always feels like this.

17:38.290 --> 17:41.530
Planning this kind of stuff is actually really fun!

17:45.740 --> 17:47.580
Riki, are the preparations done?

17:47.580 --> 17:49.280
Yeah, how are things on your end?

17:49.280 --> 17:50.760
Are you sure about that mustache?

17:50.760 --> 17:51.690
We're ready.

17:51.690 --> 17:54.380
Roger that. Okay, then let's begin!

17:58.820 --> 18:00.410
Mission start!

18:00.410 --> 18:01.980
Let's go!

18:32.200 --> 18:33.110
Onee-chan!

18:33.110 --> 18:34.080
Haruka?

18:35.520 --> 18:36.490
Behold!

18:36.490 --> 18:37.780
Kurugaya-san?

18:38.200 --> 18:39.450
Boy!

18:40.560 --> 18:41.280
Futaki-san!

18:42.080 --> 18:43.500
Riki!

18:43.500 --> 18:44.870
Wait a second, you guys!

18:45.180 --> 18:46.950
Oh no! Hurry up and bring Kanata back!

18:48.260 --> 18:54.380
Being alone was painful, so the two of us held hands.

18:50.250 --> 18:51.220
Out of my way!

18:54.480 --> 19:00.510
We were still lonely so all of us stood in a circle and joined hands.

19:00.480 --> 19:09.100
I'm sure this will become the strength of thousands,

19:07.140 --> 19:09.490
Oh, looks pretty intense in there.

19:08.700 --> 19:13.600
and make any dream come true.

19:10.200 --> 19:13.020
Was this your plan, Natsume-senpai?

19:13.020 --> 19:17.900
"You got it!" is what I would like to say, but this was all Riki and Saigusa's idea.

19:13.660 --> 19:16.360
Fly high towards the sky,

19:15.960 --> 19:20.450
Kick off the ground and send your voice to the heavens,

19:19.300 --> 19:21.280
Hang on a second~

19:20.210 --> 19:25.620
And soar past those painful days.

19:21.280 --> 19:22.740
Here you go Rin-chan!

19:24.240 --> 19:27.080
Kyousuke, Rin, I'll leave the diversion to you.

19:25.550 --> 19:30.620
I will never forget your voice or your tears.

19:27.080 --> 19:27.580
Yeah.

19:27.580 --> 19:29.330
Yeah, leave the cleanup to us.

19:29.330 --> 19:30.250
Let's go!

19:30.350 --> 19:37.710
Now our future of hope is about to begin.

19:30.800 --> 19:31.670
Don't get caught!

19:31.670 --> 19:33.140
See you later then!

19:35.940 --> 19:36.650
Wait!

19:36.650 --> 19:37.960
Haruka, wait!

19:37.480 --> 19:44.370
So despite the hardships that await, your feet will take a step forward.

19:41.440 --> 19:44.190
Do you really think they'll let us off easily?

19:44.190 --> 19:46.350
If we go back now, it may not be too late.

19:44.490 --> 19:50.230
We all had the same dream

19:47.290 --> 19:49.280
Is that what you want to do, Onee-chan?

19:49.280 --> 19:52.630
Do you want to return to that household with uncle?

19:50.160 --> 19:55.770
of that one passing page.

19:55.790 --> 20:02.950
The future only allows use to bring one page

19:56.100 --> 19:57.980
You have no reason to go back.

19:57.980 --> 19:59.910
No, I won't let you go back!

19:59.910 --> 20:02.870
That place isn't your home!

20:02.670 --> 20:09.290
Is it alright to choose that page?

20:02.870 --> 20:06.140
If you have to go back no matter what, then I'm coming with you!

20:06.140 --> 20:08.740
Everyone's coming with you!

20:09.300 --> 20:12.080
There's strength within our hearts

20:09.880 --> 20:12.610
What nonsense are you...

20:11.680 --> 20:14.290
An unmatched strength.

20:12.610 --> 20:14.370
It's fine. I've already decided.

20:14.100 --> 20:16.750
A tear fell down our cheeks,

20:14.370 --> 20:16.360
I've already decided to do this.

20:16.360 --> 20:18.960
If I had to choose, this ending is better.

20:16.480 --> 20:19.300
a single tear.

20:18.960 --> 20:22.380
If I had to choose, this kind of ending is better than a sad one.

20:20.440 --> 20:23.220
Fly high towards the sky,

20:22.820 --> 20:27.220
Kick off the ground and send your voice to the heavens,

20:23.080 --> 20:25.760
It's obvious this is better.

20:27.030 --> 20:32.180
And soar past those painful days.

20:27.570 --> 20:28.790
Well, what will you do?

20:32.160 --> 20:37.400
I will never forget your voice or your tears.

20:34.980 --> 20:37.480
I've... never wished for any of this...

20:37.120 --> 20:44.280
Now our future of hope is about to begin.

20:41.140 --> 20:42.940
I've never wished for this, and yet...

20:44.160 --> 20:46.370
I was just being self-centered.

20:44.260 --> 20:50.660
So despite the hardships that await, your feet will take a step forward.

20:46.370 --> 20:49.100
I really hate myself for being so self-centered.

20:49.990 --> 20:54.330
I said all those things, but here I am clinging to you guys.

20:50.640 --> 21:01.480
Let us believe that we'll be able to overcome all trials.

20:55.050 --> 20:56.350
It's fine.

20:56.350 --> 20:59.170
We came here to help you, after all.

20:59.940 --> 21:01.770
It's the same for all of us.

21:01.770 --> 21:03.970
We all came to save you.

21:04.570 --> 21:05.990
Why?

21:05.990 --> 21:09.720
Why do all of you guys reach your hands out to people so easily?

21:10.460 --> 21:12.850
We know we all have small hands.

21:13.660 --> 21:17.310
We always feel like we're about to get crushed.

21:17.370 --> 21:22.650
But that's why we join our hands together, and reach out to other people.

21:23.430 --> 21:26.610
That's how the Little Busters were formed.

21:27.250 --> 21:29.570
It’s because we’re weak individually

21:29.570 --> 21:31.360
that we stick together.

21:33.820 --> 21:35.250
Kanata...

21:48.960 --> 21:51.210
I don't want to go back.

21:51.210 --> 21:53.060
I really don't want to go back!

21:53.920 --> 21:58.690
I want to be with Haruka... With everyone...

22:06.500 --> 22:17.660
Under those scarlet clouds, two of my memories start to drift far away.

22:12.510 --> 22:15.030
That was a real mess.

22:15.900 --> 22:18.600
Guess you'll just have to hide until the heat dies down.

22:18.020 --> 22:25.050
Among the echoes of a bell chime, we both take a piece.

22:19.360 --> 22:22.500
The truth is, I already submitted a form of absence.

22:23.390 --> 22:24.380
For the two of us.

22:24.380 --> 22:25.460
Eh?

22:24.770 --> 22:29.300
I hope the sun will be out tomorrow.

22:25.460 --> 22:29.550
Hey, let's live together. In mom and dad's house.

22:28.980 --> 22:33.680
I wonder if we can make it beyond the stars?

22:33.410 --> 22:40.480
As I walk, I look up at the sky and see a single light.

22:40.160 --> 22:45.440
Even if I'm all alone above the moon,

22:45.210 --> 22:53.200
I'll run towards the end of this spiral.

22:53.300 --> 22:59.750
You said that I would be able to smile after I cried.

22:59.520 --> 23:05.340
I won't ever forget our journey.

23:04.940 --> 23:11.090
I'll cast a spell so you won't forget, and I won't say goodbye.

23:10.860 --> 23:17.430
You'll be able to walk forward again someday
